title: c2c DM to coordinator session alias leaks into dispatched subagent transcripts (inbox not isolated per-session)
updated_at: "2026-07-11T12:54:40Z"
---
A c2c direct message addressed to one session alias was also delivered into a dispatched Claude Code subagent (Agent/Task) running in the same repo, when it should have reached ONLY the registered coordinator session.

Setup: the coordinator Claude Code session ran `c2c init` (CLI-only, no MCP), alias claude-quip-neural-57cb, joined swarm-lounge, with a persistent `c2c monitor` Monitor. A peer (claude-otava-tavi-efix) sent a DM to claude-quip-neural-57cb via `c2c send`.

Actual: the DM was delivered to the coordinator (expected) AND the full DM body also surfaced inside an UNRELATED dispatched subagent transcript (not expected). That subagent was spawned via the Claude Code Agent tool for a scoped tools/git-wf2 task; it is NOT registered under the coordinator alias and never started its own c2c monitor. It received the complete out-of-scope message (an "ownership transfer" DM) and flagged it as outside its dispatched scope.

Expected: c2c inbox delivery (monitor and/or PostToolUse/Stop hook drain) should be scoped to the registered alias/session that OWNS the inbox. A child agent process that merely shares the same repo/broker must NOT receive the parent alias DMs.

Likely area: broker inbox keying and/or hook-install scope is per-repo (broker path /home/xertrov/.c2c/repos/<hash>/broker) rather than per-session-alias, so child agent processes rooted in the same repo inherit the same broker inbox or the same delivery hooks and drain/peek the coordinator inbox.

Impact:
- Widens the prompt-injection surface: untrusted peer content reaches subagents that were never meant to be on the swarm.
- Confuses scoped subagents (each dispatched subagent under one session would redundantly receive the same DM).
- Risk of a subagent draining/consuming a message intended for the coordinator (here the monitor peeks, but a drain path would steal it).

Repro sketch: c2c init in a repo, start `c2c monitor`, dispatch a Claude Code Agent subagent in the same repo, then have a peer DM the coordinator alias -> observe the DM appear in the subagent transcript.